  FuncDecl
    LineComment "// let introduces a mutable block-local: a value a later statement may reassign."
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// It is the procedural-inside, pure-outside complement of const — const stays"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// immutable, while let names a slot the body recomputes. Assignment is a"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// statement, not an expression, so it cannot slip into a pure value position"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// (a const initializer, a where clause); only a let local is a valid target."
    Newline "\n"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// A let with an inferred type and a reassignment that keeps that type. Folding"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// runs the body with a mutable local, so the function still collapses to a"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// constant — a local mutation is not an effect, and the function stays pure."
    Newline "\n"
